    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0170" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1943China/pg160"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Generalissimo Chiang
                            Kai-shek to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="94" xml:id="d126-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-11-09">November 9,
                        1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>No. 858. Mme Chiang down with flu and dysentery. Funeral of late President Lin
                    Sen scheduled for 17th. Provided Mme Chiang <pb facs="0171" n="161"
                        xml:id="pg161"/> has recovered I intend to leave here early on the 18th.
                    Otherwise I must delay my departure, in which case your conference with Stalin
                    can take place before ours. I prefer seeing you before you see Stalin and
                    sincerely hope our plans will work out in that way.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chiang Kai-shek</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
